{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014XtwThmsaNe2jkCkrtCiDt","type":"tool_result","content":"commit d885d0c4a7748bd84270792ce6a73625edda3af9\nAuthor: Reviewer <reviewer@example.test>\nDate:   Thu Oct 8 18:44:25 2026 -0500\n\n    build: WI-860: a review's scope excludes defects that need a compromised host\n    \n    PROCESS.md §6 states the review threat model in one paragraph, its one\n    home (the owner's 2026-10-08 ruling, rule 1): a review hunts defects in a\n    normal working environment (agent-written repository content, supported\n    configurations, regressions); a finding needing a compromised or contrived\n    host is dismissed in one recorded line and never answered with code. The\n    reviewer brief links it through {process_doc} §6, restating nothing; no\n    adjudication brief judges a review finding today (WI-865 adds one). The\n    prompt catalog regenerated, the byte-budget rows re-stamped (+652 bytes),\n    and a RESYNC entry added.\n    \n    Builder (Claude Opus, kit-builder): red 1 failed on the new test; green 229\n    passed, 1 skipped on the affected modules; smoke 2377 passed, 2 skipped;\n    check_docs 0 broken; catalog fresh.\n    \n    WI: WI-860\n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\ndiff --git a/project-trajectory/PROCESS.md b/project-trajectory/PROCESS.md\nindex 68bde243..02c14409 100644\n--- a/project-trajectory/PROCESS.md\n+++ b/project-trajectory/PROCESS.md\n@@ -1002,6 +1002,16 @@ flowchart TD\n   their own claims; that class needs the independent reviewer.)\n - **Low/mechanical** (rename, doc tweak, config): just run the harness.\n \n+**Review threat model.** A review hunts defects in a normal working\n+environment: the content agents write into the repository (the gates exist to\n+check it), supported configurations, and regressions of supported behavior.\n+A finding whose reproduction needs the host itself compromised or contrived (a\n+fake or hostile binary, a shim